= Resource Description Framework — Simple =

'''RDF''' is a way to represent information as simple statements.

Each statement usually has three parts:

<pre>
subject → relation → object
</pre>

Example:

<pre>
Mars → orbits → Sun
</pre>

Many statements together form a graph.

RDF is used in the [[Semantic Web/Simple|Semantic Web]] and many [[Knowledge graph/Simple|knowledge graphs]].

RDF is not one file format.

The same RDF graph can be written as Turtle, JSON-LD, RDF/XML, and other formats.

RDF can also use shared identifiers so different datasets can talk about the same resources.

